---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { articleContentClasses } from '../styles/article-classes';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How I use analytics on this site and what gets sent when you visit."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <div class:list={[articleContentClasses, 'mt-8']}>
      <p>
        I use Google Analytics to understand aggregate page traffic on this site. It measures standard page visits only;
        the site does not define custom analytics events or send form content, resume-export content, custom user
        identifiers, or advertising-personalization signals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Analytics runs without analytics or advertising storage. The Google tag may send cookieless measurement pings,
        but it is instructed not to create or read analytics or advertising cookies. Page and referrer URLs are reduced
        to their origin and path before measurement, excluding query parameters and fragments.
      </p>
      <p>
        I limit analytics to public HTML pages. The content manager, error pages, and the JSON, text, and Markdown
        resume exports are excluded.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google processes the resulting measurement data under its own terms. For more information, read
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
